<Base title="Portable AI State: fictional first" description="An independent synthetic-only assistant identity and encrypted memory demo. Keys stay local; disclosure to a model is an explicit choice."><h1>Encrypted assistant state.</h1><p class="lede">Carry / forward is an independent mini-app for a fictional assistant identity and selected memories. It encrypts locally and gives you a separate, explicit disclosure step.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="https://ai.loftwah.com">Open the fictional demo</a><a href="https://github.com/loftwah/app-composer-state">Inspect the independent source</a></div><section class="section split"><div><h2>Fictional from the first byte.</h2><p>Mira Vale and the other perspectives are invented fixtures. No Emilio data or real sensitive personal records are used. The encrypted document, owner-held passphrase and model disclosure are separate objects.</p><p>Round-trip, wrong-key, tampering and scoped-disclosure tests are necessary evidence. They are not a substitute for the complete security, provider interoperability and recovery gates.</p></div><div class="ink"><h3>A clear privacy boundary</h3><p>No provider or storage-server requests. Optional device persistence stores ciphertext only. Copying reviewed context is a deliberate plaintext disclosure to the clipboard and whatever model you choose.</p><p><a href="/release">Check the actual acceptance state</a></p></div></section></Base>
